    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "root = [3, 1, 4, null, 2], k = 1               ->  1\nroot = [5, 3, 6, 2, 4, null, null, 1], k = 3   ->  3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Full in-order list"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function kthSmallest(root, k) {\n  const values = [];\n  const inorder = (node) => {\n    if (node === null) return;\n    inorder(node.left);\n    values.push(node.val);\n    inorder(node.right);\n  };\n  inorder(root);\n  return values[k - 1];                    // the list is sorted\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def kth_smallest(root, k):\n    values = []\n\n    def inorder(node):\n        if node is None:\n            return\n        inorder(node.left)\n        values.append(node.val)\n        inorder(node.right)\n\n    inorder(root)\n    return values[k - 1]                  # the list is sorted"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int kthSmallest(TreeNode root, int k) {\n    List<Integer> values = new ArrayList<>();\n    inorder(root, values);\n    return values.get(k - 1);                        // the list is sorted\n}\n\nvoid inorder(TreeNode node, List<Integer> values) {\n    if (node == null) return;\n    inorder(node.left, values);\n    values.add(node.val);\n    inorder(node.right, values);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "void inorder(TreeNode* node, vector<int>& values) {\n    if (node == nullptr) return;\n    inorder(node->left, values);\n    values.push_back(node->val);\n    inorder(node->right, values);\n}\n\nint kthSmallest(TreeNode* root, int k) {\n    vector<int> values;\n    inorder(root, values);\n    return values[k - 1];                            // the list is sorted\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(n).** Simple, but it walks the whole tree even when k = 1."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Iterative in-order that stops at k"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "kth-smallest-bst",
      "caption": "Push the left spine, pop the smallest, count it, then move into its right subtree."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function kthSmallest(root, k) {\n  const stack = [];\n  let node = root;\n  while (true) {\n    while (node !== null) {                // go as far left as possible\n      stack.push(node);\n      node = node.left;\n    }\n    node = stack.pop();                    // the next smallest value\n    k--;\n    if (k === 0) return node.val;\n    node = node.right;\n  }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def kth_smallest(root, k):\n    stack = []\n    node = root\n    while True:\n        while node is not None:           # go as far left as possible\n            stack.append(node)\n            node = node.left\n        node = stack.pop()                # the next smallest value\n        k -= 1\n        if k == 0:\n            return node.val\n        node = node.right"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int kthSmallest(TreeNode root, int k) {\n    Deque<TreeNode> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();\n    TreeNode node = root;\n    while (true) {\n        while (node != null) {                       // go as far left as possible\n            stack.push(node);\n            node = node.left;\n        }\n        node = stack.pop();                          // the next smallest value\n        if (--k == 0) return node.val;\n        node = node.right;\n    }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int kthSmallest(TreeNode* root, int k) {\n    stack<TreeNode*> st;\n    TreeNode* node = root;\n    while (true) {\n        while (node != nullptr) {                    // go as far left as possible\n            st.push(node);\n            node = node->left;\n        }\n        node = st.top();                             // the next smallest value\n        st.pop();\n        if (--k == 0) return node->val;\n        node = node->right;\n    }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(h + k), space O(h).** It touches only the left spine plus the k values it counts."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "3. Count subtree sizes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Let `size(left)` be the number of nodes in the left subtree. If k ≤ size(left), the answer is on the left. If k = size(left) + 1, it's this node. Otherwise it's the (k − size(left) − 1)-th smallest on the right."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function kthSmallest(root, k) {\n  const size = (node) => (node === null ? 0 : 1 + size(node.left) + size(node.right));\n  let node = root;\n  while (true) {\n    const left = size(node.left);\n    if (k <= left) node = node.left;\n    else if (k === left + 1) return node.val;\n    else {\n      k -= left + 1;                       // skip the left side and this node\n      node = node.right;\n    }\n  }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def kth_smallest(root, k):\n    def size(node):\n        return 0 if node is None else 1 + size(node.left) + size(node.right)\n\n    node = root\n    while True:\n        left = size(node.left)\n        if k <= left:\n            node = node.left\n        elif k == left + 1:\n            return node.val\n        else:\n            k -= left + 1                 # skip the left side and this node\n            node = node.right"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int kthSmallest(TreeNode root, int k) {\n    TreeNode node = root;\n    while (true) {\n        int left = size(node.left);\n        if (k <= left) node = node.left;\n        else if (k == left + 1) return node.val;\n        else {\n            k -= left + 1;                           // skip the left side and this node\n            node = node.right;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nint size(TreeNode node) {\n    return node == null ? 0 : 1 + size(node.left) + size(node.right);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int size(TreeNode* node) {\n    return node == nullptr ? 0 : 1 + size(node->left) + size(node->right);\n}\n\nint kthSmallest(TreeNode* root, int k) {\n    TreeNode* node = root;\n    while (true) {\n        int left = size(node->left);\n        if (k <= left) node = node->left;\n        else if (k == left + 1) return node->val;\n        else {\n            k -= left + 1;                           // skip the left side and this node\n            node = node->right;\n        }\n    }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n·h) here, space O(h)** — recounting sizes is expensive. But if every node **stores** its subtree size (updated on insert and delete), each query is just one walk down: **O(h)**. That's the answer to the interview follow-up \"what if the tree is modified often and kthSmallest is called often?\" — an **order-statistic tree**."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Full in-order list",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "It walks the **whole tree**, even when k = 1.",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "The list holds **every value**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Iterative in-order that stops at k",
          "time": "O(h + k)",
          "timeWhy": "It walks the **left spine (h)**, then counts only **k** values before stopping.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "The stack holds **one path**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Count subtree sizes",
          "time": "O(h)",
          "timeWhy": "With **stored** subtree sizes, each step picks a side in O(1): one walk down. (Recounting sizes every time costs O(n·h).)",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "The walk or recursion along **one path**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
